  "seoTitle": "MPR Sets Schedule To Select New Vice President",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian parliament prepares to select a new vice president following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka, with a target date before December 5.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The People's Consultative Assembly of Indonesia is scheduling a plenary session to finalize the selection of a new vice president.",
    "President Prabowo Subianto is required to submit two potential candidates to the parliament within a 14-day window following the vacancy.",
    "Political parties in the governing coalition have expressed support for the president's decision-making process regarding the replacements."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the resignation of Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka, the Indonesian government has entered a constitutional process to appoint a successor. President Prabowo Subianto holds the authority to nominate two candidates to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) for consideration. Parliamentary leadership has indicated that the selection process is expected to conclude before December 5, 2026, with the plenary session likely occurring between November 23 and December 4. Government officials, including the Coordinating Minister for Law, Human Rights, Immigration, and Correctional Affairs, have emphasized the importance of rigorous document verification for candidates to ensure legal compliance. Various political factions, including the National Mandate Party (PAN), the Prosperous Justice Party (PKS), and the National Awakening Party (PKB), have stated they will support the president's selection process through coalition consultation.",
